{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you shall set them.</b> There were three forms there: one for shaping while it is dough, one for baking it inside in the oven, and one that he places them in when they are baked, so that they not spoil. Two arrangements at the two ends of the table." "<b>Six arrangement upon the pure table.</b> Six loaves one atop the other at one of the two ends of the table, and six other loaves one atop the other at its other end. The width of the loaf across the width of the table and the length of the loaf along the length of the table, as I explained in the section of Terumah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:55.283565876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}